  "body": "In particular we cannot tie it to browsing contexts, as those can be discarded.\r\n```\r\nconst frame = self[0]\r\nalert(frame.menubar)\r\nframe.frameElement.remove()\r\nalert(frame.menubar)\r\n```\r\nFirefox: obj, obj\r\nSafari TP: obj, undefined\r\nChrome: obj, obj\r\nEdge: obj, exception (\"Object expected\")\r\n\r\nIn Firefox and Chrome visible will return false for the case lacking a browsing context. That's probably what we should go with.",
